---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const repoUrl = "https://github.com/rpivo/gerrymandering-map";
---

<Base
  title="Gerrymandering Map"
  description="Every US congressional district, its shape, and how irregular that shape is."
>
  <main>
    <p class="eyebrow">Work in progress</p>
    <h1>Gerrymandering Map</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every US congressional district, what it looks like, and how irregular its shape is
      compared with all the others.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="coming">
      <h2 id="coming">Coming soon</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Outlines of all 435 districts, searchable by state, district or representative.</li>
        <li>
          An irregularity score from 0 to 100 for each one, based on three standard measures
          of compactness.
        </li>
        <li>A plain-language explanation of what the scores can and can't tell you.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="note">
      A score describes a district's shape, not the intent behind it. Coastlines, rivers and
      the Voting Rights Act can all make a district irregular for good reasons.
    </p>

    <p><a href={repoUrl}>Follow along on GitHub</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .note {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
